  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 518.18 Record Keeping",
  "priorExpiration": "2012-03-15",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 518.18 Record Keeping.\n\n(a) Each municipal agent shall keep a record of all registration certificates issued by the municipal agent or any employee, including:\n\n(1) The date of registration;\n\n(2) The last name of the registrant;\n\n(3) The registration number; and\n\n(4) The inventory issued.\n\n(b) Each record shall be kept so as to compile all information necessary to complete the summaries required by Saf-C 518.16(a)(2).\n\n(c) No municipal agent or employee(s) shall refuse or fail to provide the director, any auditor, or other person authorized by the director, with any records relating to the registration of any vehicles. The director may take the records in hand for inspection, or in order to photocopy.\n\n(d) Any inspection conducted in accordance with this section shall be in compliance with RSA 261:74-e.\n\nSource. #7972, eff 10-17-03 (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Saf-C 500); ss by #9995, INTERIM, eff 9-17-11, EXPIRED: 3-15-12\n\nNew. #10135, eff 5-23-12; ss by #13521, eff 1-13-23 (formerly Saf-C 519.18)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c500.html"
